  "_about": "The world: regions, roads, where the player starts, shrines, named locations (for quests and the map), and where npcs, enemies and loot are placed. Positions are [x, z] in metres; north is -z. `water`: ponds you can fish (a loot table of fish). `obscured`: areas too dark to enter without a torch. `chests`: chests to open, with `items`, `coins` (silver) and an optional `lock` ({key: item id, pick: Lockpicking rank}). placedLoot with `respawn` (seconds) is a gathering node: it grows back after it is taken; `scale` resizes its model; `quest` makes it takeable (and sparkle) only while that quest is active and still needs the item.",
